BODY = [
("p", "Cristiano Ronaldo has retired from international football, ending 23 years with Portugal as the highest scorer and most-capped player in the history of the men's game."),
("p", "The 41-year-old announced it on Thursday, 5 November 2026, in a video on Instagram captioned <em>\"Portugal estará sempre em mim\"</em>: Portugal will always be in me. In it, he spoke of handing back the national team's number seven shirt, saying he never felt it belonged to him alone."),
("p", "He said he leaves \"with my head held high\" and proud of the road he took. He thanked his teammates, his coaches, his family and Portuguese supporters around the world, and looked back on the sacrifices, the wins and the defeats along the way."),
("p", "It is the end of one of the great international careers. It is also the end of a messy few weeks, and the two stories are hard to separate."),
("h2", "The summer", "After the ", "World Cup"),
("p", "The questions started in the summer. Portugal went out of the 2026 World Cup in the round of 16, beaten 1-0 by Spain on 6 July, and Ronaldo confirmed that it had been his last World Cup."),
("p", "He did not walk away then. Over the summer he held off on any decision about his international future, and he later admitted he had thought about leaving after the World Cup. After talks with the federation's president and the new coach, he said he still believed he could help the team."),
("p", "Roberto Martínez stepped down after the defeat. On 10 July, the Portuguese Football Federation (FPF) named Jorge Jesus as the new head coach, a man who already knew Ronaldo well from Al Nassr and who made it clear he would welcome him back. Ronaldo stayed in the squad, and for a moment it looked like a smooth handover."),
("h2", "27 September", "The night in ", "Oslo"),
("p", "It unravelled on 27 September. Portugal beat Norway 2-1 in Oslo in the Nations League, and Ronaldo spent the whole match on the bench."),
("p", "At full time, he walked straight to the dressing room. He did not join his teammates in applauding the Portugal fans who had travelled to Norway."),
("p", "The two men's accounts of what went wrong differ. Ronaldo says Jesus told him he would come on, so he began warming up, only for the coach to change his mind. Jesus has insisted that keeping him on the bench was a tactical decision, not a broken promise."),
("p", "Days later, with the squad based in Copenhagen ahead of a Nations League game against Denmark, Ronaldo left the camp. He has said he told the federation before he went."),
("h2", "The fallout", "A ban, a fine ", "and an apology"),
("p", "The FPF opened disciplinary proceedings on 9 October. Ronaldo apologised to his teammates and supporters, admitted he should not have left, and said he would accept whatever punishment came while still wanting to play for Portugal."),
("p", "On 19 October, the federation's disciplinary council handed him a 30-day suspension and a €255 fine. FPF president Pedro Proença said everyone at the federation wanted him back once it was resolved."),
("p", "In the end, he chose not to come back."),
("h2", "2003 to 2026", "The record ", "he leaves"),
("p", "Whatever the manner of the exit, the numbers are untouched. No man has scored more international goals, and no man has played more international matches."),
("facts", [("Debut", "2003"), ("Caps", "234 (men's record)"), ("Goals", "146 (men's record)"), ("Major titles", "Euro 2016; Nations League 2019 and 2025")]),
("p", "The overall international scoring record belongs to Canada's Christine Sinclair, with 190 goals."),
("p", "Euro 2016 is the title that defines his Portugal years. He went off injured early in the final in Paris, and Portugal still beat hosts France 1-0 after extra time for the country's first major trophy. The Nations League wins followed in 2019 and 2025, the second against Spain on penalties."),
("h2", "What now", "What comes ", "next"),
("p", "Ronaldo is not retiring from football. He plays on at Al Nassr in Saudi Arabia, and the chase for 1,000 career goals goes on without international matches to help it along."),
("p", "The Ronaldo name has not left Portugal's set-up, either. His son, Cristiano Jr, earned his first call-up to Portugal's under-15s in May 2025 and to the under-16s that October."),
("p", "For Portugal, it is a strange new beginning. For the first time since 2003, the national team will plan for a future without Cristiano Ronaldo in it, and the number seven shirt he spoke of handing back is waiting for someone brave enough to take it."),
]

